  "reading": "Headroom is the fraction of problems the model can already solve somewhere in k samples but does not solve greedily. That is exactly the set a rejection-sampling round would harvest and train on. Near zero headroom means the run is not worth spending.",
  "non_claims": [
    "pass@6 counts the 6 SAMPLES only. The separate union column adds problems solved only by the greedy decode. An earlier version of this receipt reported the union as pass@6, inflating it to 0.7083 against the true 0.6667; the `power` task is the proof, with a union cell of 0.333 and a per-sample rate of 0.000. Headroom is union minus greedy and is unchanged.",
    "n=3 per task; per-task headroom below roughly 56 points is noise.",
    "pass@k is an upper bound on what rejection sampling can harvest, not a prediction of what a fine-tune would reach.",
    "Sampling was added here; every shipped decode path is argmax. These temperature and top-k settings are a first guess, not a tuned choice."
  ],
  "corrected": "2026-09-03: pass_at_k separated from the greedy union"
